.TH IMUD\-PROMETHEUS.CONF 5 "2026-08-05" "imud 1.8.2" "File Formats Manual"
.SH NAME
imud\-prometheus.conf \- configuration for the imud Prometheus exporter
.SH SYNOPSIS
.I /etc/imud/imud\-prometheus.conf
.SH DESCRIPTION
TOML-style key/value file read by
.BR imud\-prometheus (8)
at startup and on SIGHUP. The exporter reads only this file, never
.IR imud.conf .
Keys marked [restart] require a service restart to take effect.
.SH "SECTION [imud-prometheus]"
.TP
.B enabled
.RI (bool,\ default:\ true)
Run the exporter daemon. With it true and
.B http_enabled
false the daemon runs but does not bind the /metrics port; set it false to not
run the exporter at all (it exits cleanly, so systemd does not restart it). [restart]
.TP
.B http_enabled
.RI (bool,\ default:\ false)
Serve the /metrics HTTP listener (the exporter's only output). [restart]
.TP
.B socket
.RI (string,\ default:\ /run/imud/imud\-stream.sock)
Path of imud's [stream] AF_UNIX socket to read. [restart]
.TP
.B listen_addr
.RI (string,\ default:\ 127.0.0.1)
HTTP bind address. Set
.B 0.0.0.0
to allow scrapes from another host. [restart]
.TP
.B listen_port
.RI (int,\ default:\ 9815)
HTTP port for
.BR GET\ /metrics .
[restart]
.SH "SECTION [logging]"
.TP
.B level
.RI (string,\ default:\ info)
error | warn | info | debug. Reloaded on SIGHUP.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/imud/imud-prometheus.conf
This file.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR imud\-prometheus (8),
.BR imud.conf (5),
.BR imud (8)
